[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was marked known as one issue with one fix queued. The reports merged
into it describe more than one problem, so each problem got its own ticket. Engineering closed
#4471 on 5 October: the parser is fixed, and the hint will not be fixed because the booking-v3 form
is retired.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix does not explain a date that moves by one day. If one-day moves keep coming in,
reopen #3.
</Callout>

## The problems

The counts are the desk's own: the cause table from the #4471 page, on the export as it came.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

- `parser`, [#1](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/1), the `parser` row. Closed as fixed by
  `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The shared parser read every date month first, so a
  tenant that writes the day first got day and month swapped. "Our 7 April reminder went out on
  4 July." It came in by every channel, from every tenant.
- `hint`, [#2](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/2), the `hint` row. Closed as won't fix: the booking-v3
  form is retired. The form printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, then read the date day
  first, the tenant's way. People typed what the hint said and got the same swap. Only form reports
  from booking-v3 tenants, and the parser fix did not reach this form. The table says it has no
  ticket of its own; #2 is that ticket.
- `one-day move`, [#3](https://github.com/dudziakm/mega-s01e03-support-kb/issues/3), the note under the table. Closed with the parser
  fix, because the desk files these reports under `parser` by tenant and counts them there, so #1
  includes them. Here the date moves by one day, while day and month stay where they are: "Invite
  says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in
  Toronto got Monday."

## How the desk counts

1. One id, one report: the export repeats reports where its pages overlap.
2. A report goes under its tenant's cause (`causes.ts`): a form report from a booking-v3 tenant
   that writes the day first is `hint`; any other report from a day-first tenant is `parser`.
3. A report the desk read differently (its notes) stays counted where it is filed, with a note
   under the table.

Intake's tag is not used: it guesses from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant.

## Why one ticket held them all

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match. The
same subject lines come in for different problems, so matching on subjects cannot keep these
problems apart. Changing that rule needs a new decision record; 0001 stays as accepted.

## When the export changes

The table reads the ticket export and the desk notes at render time, so a newer export changes the
counts on this page without an edit. The counts in the tickets are from the export of 4 October.

